crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:18:10: error: cannot take the gradient of `loose`: its parameter `x` has no unit
   |
18 | a = grad(loose)(1 m, 2 m)
   |          ^^^^^ the gradient is with respect to every parameter
 3 | def loose(x, y: m) -> m:
   |     ----- `loose` is defined here
   = note: each derivative has the unit of the result divided by the unit of its parameter, and an unannotated parameter accepts any unit
   = help: annotate the parameter with its unit, for example `x: m`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:19:10: error: cannot take the gradient of `norm`: its parameter `v` is not a scalar
   |
19 | b = grad(norm)([1 m, 2 m, 3 m])
   |          ^^^^ the gradient is with respect to every parameter
 6 | def norm(v: Vector[3] m) -> m:
   |             ----------- this is Vector[3] [L]
   = note: differentiation does not go through arrays yet, so a gradient is with respect to scalar parameters
   = help: take the components as scalar parameters, for example `def norm(x: m, y: m, z: m)`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:20:10: error: cannot differentiate `path`: its result is Vector[3] [L], not a number
   |
20 | d = grad(path)(1 s)
   |          ^^^^ this function's result
 9 | def path(t: s) -> Vector[3] m:
   |     ---- `path` is defined here
   = note: the derivative of an array-valued function is a Jacobian, which comes with arrays at run time

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:21:10: error: `grad` needs a function defined with `def`, found the built-in `sqrt`
   |
21 | e = grad(sqrt)(4)
   |          ^^^^ a built-in function
   = note: a `def` states the units of its parameters and result, which the unit of the derivative is computed from
   = help: wrap it in a `def` that states its units, and take the gradient of that

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:22:5: error: `grad` takes 1 argument, found 2: a function
   |
22 | f = grad(position, t)(1 s)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ extra argument
   = note: the gradient is with respect to every parameter, so no parameter is named
   = help: write `grad(f)(...)` for all of them, or `derivative(f, x)(...)` for one parameter

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:23:5: error: `grad` takes 1 argument, found 0: a function
   |
23 | g = grad()(1 s)
   |     ^^^^^^ missing argument
   = help: write `grad(f)(...)`, then the arguments of `f`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:24:10: error: cannot take the gradient of `constant`: it has no parameters
   |
24 | h = grad(constant)()
   |          ^^^^^^^^ nothing to differentiate with respect to
12 | def constant() -> m:
   |     -------- `constant` is defined here
   = help: give the function the parameters the gradient is taken with respect to

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:25:5: error: `grad(position)` is a function, and must be called where it is written
   |
25 | i = grad(position)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not called
   = note: Sky has no function values yet: a function can be called, but not stored or passed around
   = help: pass the arguments of the function: `grad(position)(...)`, or name the gradient with a `def` that calls it

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:26:10: error: `grad` needs a function defined with `def`, found another derivative
   |
26 | j = grad(derivative(position, t))(1 s)
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `derivative(...)`, which can only be called
   = help: name the first derivative with a `def` that calls it, and take the gradient of that

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_grad_forms.sky:27:16: error: `derivative` needs a function defined with `def`, found a gradient
   |
27 | k = derivative(grad(position), t)(1 s)
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `grad(...)`, which can only be called
   = help: name the first gradient with a `def` that calls it, and differentiate that

